Author: Phu.le <phulealali@gmail.com>
Date:   Mon Oct 19 06:37:14 2026 +0700

    test(shellx-core): deterministic sealed-invite tamper tests
    
    The standard-alphabet case re-encoded a fresh random 93-byte blob with
    STANDARD. 93 is a multiple of 3 (no padding), so whenever the URL-safe
    string had no '-' or '_' (about (62/64)^124 = 2%) the "tampered" string was
    byte-identical to the valid one and opened. Product code is correct.
    Move that case onto the pinned known-answer blob, which contains '-', and
    also check '/' and a positive control.

